      "Requisition§God-Emperor’s Due": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 2
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition in the Determine Victor step, if you gained 5 or more Honour points during that battle and you were not the victor. You gain the Victor bonus described in that mission even though you were not the victor."
      },
      "Requisition§Penitent Crusade": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition at the end of an Oathsworn Campaign, if one or more of the following applies to your Crusade force:\n\nYou lost more battles during that Oathsworn Campaign than you won.\n\nOne or more ADEPTUS ASTARTES CHARACTER units from your Order of Battle have one or more of the following Battle Scars: Battle-weary; Disgraced; Mark of Shame.\n\nAn EMPEROR’S CHAMPION model from your Crusade army was destroyed in one of the battles fought during that Oathsworn Campaign, and at the end of that battle you lost 5 Honour points as a result of the Recovering Sacred Wargear Agenda.\n\nThe next Oathsworn Campaign you start will be a Penitent Crusade. At the end of that Oathsworn Campaign, if you have 10 or more Honour points, each ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit on your Order of Battle gains 1XP and you can select one of the following rewards:\n\nGain an additional 10 Honour points.\n\nGain 5 Relic Fragments.\n\nRemove all instances of the Battle-weary, Disgraced and Mark of Shame Battle Scars from ADEPTUS ASTARTES units on your Order of Battle.\n\nHowever, at the end of that Oathsworn Campaign, if you have 9 or fewer Honour points, your Penitent Crusade fails and you must halve your Honour points gained during that Oathsworn Campaign."
      },
      "Requisition§Dogmatic Edification": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition before a battle. Select one CRUSADER SQUAD unit from your Order of Battle, and select one Battle Trait that unit has. Replace that Battle Trait with a new Black Templars Battle Trait of your choosing (this must be a Battle Honour that unit can have)."
      },
      "Requisition§Appointed to the Household": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition after a battle. Select one of the following:\n\nSelect one CRUSADER SQUAD unit on your Order of Battle with the Blooded rank or higher. Remove that unit from your Order of Battle and spend 5 Honour points to add one SWORD BRETHREN unit to your Order of Battle.\n\nSelect one CRUSADER SQUAD unit on your Order of Battle with the Blooded rank or higher. Remove that unit from your Order of Battle and spend 10 Honour points to add one SWORD BRETHREN unit to your Order of Battle and one new CRUSADER SQUAD unit to your Order of Battle.\n\nWhen a unit is replaced in this way, each new unit starts with the same XP, Battle Honours and Battle Scars as the unit it replaced and until it is removed from your Order of Battle, each time it gains XP from Dealers of Death, that new unit gains 2XP instead of 1XP. You cannot purchase this Requisition if doing so would cause your Crusade force to exceed its current Supply Limit."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Puritanical Crusader": {
        "text": "You have completed one or more Oathsworn Campaign and promoted one or more units to Chapter Command.\nYou have won three or more battles."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Blessed Executioner": {
        "text": "You have completed two or more Oathsworn Campaigns and promoted two or more units to Chapter Command.\nYour Order of Battle contains one EMPEROR’S CHAMPION model.\nYou have won six or more battles.\nOne or more units on your Order of Battle have the RELIC BEARER keyword."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Disciple of Sigismund": {
        "text": "You have completed five or more Oathsworn Campaigns and promoted three or more units to Chapter Command.\nYou have added a new unit to your army using the Appointed to the Household Requisition.\nYou have won ten or more battles.\nThree or more units on your Order of Battle have the RELIC BEARER keyword."
      },
      "Black Templars Crusade§Relic Fragments": {
        "text": "**Relic Bearers.** After an Oathsworn Campaign ends, spend Relic Fragments on Reclaimed Relics for BLACK TEMPLARS INFANTRY units of Blooded rank or higher (not CHARACTERS): one per unit, each unique; the bearer gains the RELIC BEARER keyword. Track Relic Fragments gained on this card; the Reclaimed Relics on your units spend them.\n\n**Anoint a Champion.** When your Black Templars Crusade force starts an Oathsworn Campaign you can add one EMPEROR’S CHAMPION to your Order of Battle; its points do not count towards Supply Used (but do count in any Crusade army) and it leaves when the campaign ends. It cannot earn XP or Battle Honours: at the end of each battle it gains one Champion’s Virtue (choose, or roll two D6 and gain both). Each enemy CHARACTER it destroys earns 1 Honour point. When it is destroyed, take its Out of Action test at once: if failed it is slain and removed; place a Sacred Wargear objective marker where it fell and use the Recovering Sacred Wargear Agenda (the player controlling the marker at the end of the battle gives one unit within range 3XP; if you do not control it you lose 5 Honour points). You cannot anoint another Champion until a new Oathsworn Campaign."
      },
      "Reclaimed Relic§Penitent's Roar": {
        "stats": {
          "Relic Fragments": {
            "value": 3
          }
        },
        "text": "This ornate pistol of unknown design can only be fired while chained to the bearer’s wrist but delivers each shot with uncanny accuracy, straight to the heart of any who would lay low the Emperor’s chosen crusaders.\n\nSelect one Pistol weapon equipped by the bearer that has the word ‘bolt’ in its name, e.g. bolt pistol (excluding a weapon that has been upgraded with a Weapon Modification - if you cannot do so, you cannot select this Reclaimed Relic Battle Honour). That weapon is now a Crusade Relic; it has the [precision] and [ignores cover] abilities and improve its Damage and Armour Penetration characteristics by 1.",
        "rules": {
          "relicBearer": {
            "actions": [
              {
                "actionType": "add",
                "iterations": 1,
                "paths": [
                  [
                    "{parent}",
                    "keywords",
                    "Keywords"
                  ]
                ],
                "value": "Relic Bearer"
              }
            ],
            "evals": [],
            "evaluate": "AND",
            "failState": "pass"
          }
        }
      },
